g Aid Accepting Loans Paying Your Bills Maintaining Eligibility Canceling or Changing Your Aid FAFSA Financial Aid Policies Return of Federal Funds Tuition Refund Satisfactory Academic Progress Financial Aid Fraud Scholarships & Grants Graduate Aid Working Families Program Partnership Discounts Net Price Calculator Forms & Resources FAQ Athletics Student Life Health & Wellness Counseling Nurse Emergency Care Student Health Insurance Student Organizations Spiritual Life Diversity and Inclusion Student Store Residence Life/Housing & Dining Housing Dining Parking Orientation Student Services Academic Resources First-Year Students Honors Program Learning & Writing Center Institutional Review Board (IRB) Math Placement Library Research Databases & Guides Research Tips Library Services Circulation Policy Copyright Policy Privacy and Confidentiality Policy Selection and Acquisitions Policy Guest Use Policy TRIO Office of Student Success Career & Professional Development Koonce Scholars Program Accessibility Resources About Marian Accreditation and Approvals Campus Map Directory Employment Founder’s Day History Media Kit Mission and Values News President Special Events State Authorization Student Consumer Information Title IX Title IX Support and Appeals Travel University Profile Adjunct Faculty Open Application Pool Brad Greenwood 2026-06-22T08:49:10-05:00 Categories: Instructional, Open Application Pool Marian University is a Catholic applied liberal arts community that welcomes diverse spiritual traditions. Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes, Marian University engages students in the education of the whole person. We embrace justice compassion and transform lives for professional service and leadership. Adjunct positions are available periodically. Once you submit an application to the open pool, you may be contacted by a member of the search committee if your qualifications meet the needs of the department. Work type: Part-time Requirements: Master’s degree in related discipline required. Previous post-secondary teaching experience or related professional experience desired. Special note for any applicant who resides outside of the State of Wisconsin: If you are selected for a role with Marian University and do not move to Wisconsin, your employment will be through Kelly Services. Application Requirements: Please submit a letter of interest, resume/CV, unofficial transcripts, and name, address and telephone number of three references to muapplicants@marianuniversity.edu . Please enter in the subject line “Adjunct” and the department you are applying for. Terms of Appointment: Fixed-term terminal with a one-semester appointment. Salary: Competitive Application Deadline: Review of files will begin immediately and continue until available positions are filled. More information about Marian University can be found by clicking HERE . Marian University is committed to building a culturally diverse employee workforce and strongly encourages women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, and veterans to apply. In order to keep our open pools up-to-date with interested applicants, this pool will hold your application until 06/30/2027 – At that time, we will open a new applicant pool. Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800-262-7426 admission@marianuniversity.edu Follow Us #Fightbluefight Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Tour Employment Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Privacy Policy Title IX Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800.262.7426 info@marianuniversity.edu Follow Us #Fightbluefight Toggle Navigation Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Visit Employment Privacy Policy Title IX Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Page load link Arabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Hmong Italian Japanese Korean Nepali Portuguese Russian Spanish Swedish Vietnamese en Go to Top"
    },
