s Paying Your Bills Maintaining Eligibility Canceling or Changing Your Aid FAFSA Financial Aid Policies Return of Federal Funds Tuition Refund Satisfactory Academic Progress Financial Aid Fraud Scholarships & Grants Graduate Aid Working Families Program Partnership Discounts Net Price Calculator Forms & Resources FAQ Athletics Student Life Health & Wellness Counseling Nurse Emergency Care Student Health Insurance Student Organizations Spiritual Life Diversity and Inclusion Student Store Residence Life/Housing & Dining Housing Dining Parking Orientation Student Services Academic Resources First-Year Students Honors Program Learning & Writing Center Institutional Review Board (IRB) Math Placement Library Research Databases & Guides Research Tips Library Services Circulation Policy Copyright Policy Privacy and Confidentiality Policy Selection and Acquisitions Policy Guest Use Policy TRIO Office of Student Success Career & Professional Development Koonce Scholars Program Accessibility Resources About Marian Accreditation and Approvals Campus Map Directory Employment Founder’s Day History Media Kit Mission and Values News President Special Events State Authorization Student Consumer Information Title IX Title IX Support and Appeals Travel University Profile Education Adjunct Brad Greenwood 2026-06-22T08:57:37-05:00 Marian University is a Catholic applied liberal arts community that values diverse spiritual traditions. Sponsored by the Congregation of the Sisters of St. Agnes, Marian University engages students in the education of the whole person. We embrace justice and compassion to transform lives for professional service and leadership in the global community. Work type: Part-time Marian University invites applicants for the position of Adjunct Professor in Education, starting August 2026 . Successful candidates will have a strong commitment to undergraduate education, student engagement and research, as well as service to the college and community. Marian University is an institution that values innovative teaching, advising and mentoring. Teaching responsibilities include courses each semester, as demand requires. Candidates should exhibit skill and enthusiasm in teaching undergraduates. Among the areas we may have openings are Early Childhood, Elementary-Middle, Cross-Categorical Special Education, and Middle-Secondary in the areas of Math, Broad Field Social Studies, and English. Primary Responsibilities: Teach courses in the discipline in our undergraduate Courses are delivered in a face-to-face, in-person format on our Fond du lac Campus. Timely communication with students Timely instruction and assessment of course material Minimum Qualifications: Master’s Degree in Education with preparation in the area in which you wish to teach; terminal degree in the discipline is preferred. At least 3 years of K-12 teaching experience within the area(s) of licensure Preferred qualifications include: Experience with in-person Higher-Education teaching. Experience in learning management system platforms Certification/Licensure in K-12 Education Availability to teach on campus classes weekdays between 8:00 m. and 4:30 p.m. Application Requirements: please submit a letter of interest, a curriculum vita, a statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial copies of transcripts, and the names, email address and telephone numbers of three references to muapplicants@marianuniversity.edu . Please place “Adjunct Professor, Education” in the subject line of the email. Terms of Appointment: open-ended, continual as needed. Salary: Competitive Application Deadline: Review of files will begin immediately and continue until available positions are filled. More information about Marian University can be found by clicking HERE . Marian University is committed to building a culturally diverse employee workforce and strongly encourages women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, and veterans to apply. EOE/Minorities/Females/Vet/Disabled Transforming lives through academic excellence, innovation and leadership. Marian University is a community committed to learning, dedicated to service and social justice, and joined together by spiritual traditions. Any offer of employment will be contingent upon the receipt of criminal background and reference check information; and the determination that the candidate remains eligible and suitable for employment. Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800-262-7426 admission@marianuniversity.edu Follow Us #Fightbluefight Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Tour Employment Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Privacy Policy Title IX Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800.262.7426 info@marianuniversity.edu Follow Us #Fightbluefight Toggle Navigation Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Visit Employment Privacy Policy Title IX Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Page load link Arabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Hmong Italian Japanese Korean Nepali Portuguese Russian Spanish Swedish Vietnamese en Go to Top"
