 education and student engagement. Marian University is an institution that values innovative teaching, advising and mentoring. Teaching responsibilities include teaching in-person and hybrid graduate nursing courses at our Fond du Lac, WI campus. Candidates should exhibit skill and enthusiasm in teaching. The courses are part of our Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) program and are designed to provide students with advanced theoretical knowledge and critical thinking skills necessary for success in the field of nursing. Primary Responsibilities: Deliver engaging and informative lectures that align with the course curriculum. Facilitate in-person class sessions. Foster a positive and inclusive learning environment that encourages student participation and interaction. Assess and evaluate student performance through assignments, exams, and class participation. Provide timely feedback and guidance to students to support their academic growth. Maintain open communication with students and be available for academic consultations and advising as needed. Collaborate with fellow instructors and course coordinators to ensure course success. Minimum Qualifications: Must have a Master’s degree in Nursing or related field. Active and unrestricted Nurse Practitioner (NP) license. Prior teaching experience in an academic setting. Strong communication and presentation skills. Ability to create a supportive and inclusive learning environment. All candidates must have authorization to work in the United States. Preferred: Familiarity with hybrid and online teaching. Application Requirements: Please submit a letter of interest, resume/CV, unofficial transcripts, and name, address and telephone number of three references to muapplicants@marianuniversity.edu . Please enter in the subject line “Adjunct, Graduate Nursing” Terms of Appointment: open-ended, continual as needed Salary: Competitive Application Deadline: Review of files will begin immediately and continue until available positions are filled. More information about Marian University can be found by clicking HERE . Marian University is committed to building a culturally diverse employee workforce and strongly encourages women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, and veterans to apply. Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800-262-7426 admission@marianuniversity.edu Follow Us #Fightbluefight Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Tour Employment Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Privacy Policy Title IX Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800.262.7426 info@marianuniversity.edu Follow Us #Fightbluefight Toggle Navigation Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Visit Employment Privacy Policy Title IX Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Page load link Arabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Hmong Italian Japanese Korean Nepali Portuguese Russian Spanish Swedish Vietnamese en Go to Top"
