 Policy Guest Use Policy TRIO Office of Student Success Career & Professional Development Koonce Scholars Program Accessibility Resources About Marian Accreditation and Approvals Campus Map Directory Employment Founder’s Day History Media Kit Mission and Values News President Special Events State Authorization Student Consumer Information Title IX Title IX Support and Appeals Travel University Profile Adjunct Professor, Social Work Brad Greenwood 2026-08-13T13:59:17-05:00 Position: Adjunct Professor, Social Work (Part-time, Non-Tenure Track) Department: Social Behavioral Science Reports To: Department Chair FLSA: Exempt Marian University is a Catholic applied liberal arts community that values diverse spiritual traditions. Sponsored by the Congregation of the Sisters of St. Agnes, Marian University engages students in the education of the whole person. We embrace justice and compassion to transform lives for professional service and leadership in the global community. Marian University invites applicants for the position of Adjunct Professor in Social Work, starting August 2026 . Successful candidates will have a strong commitment to undergraduate education, student engagement and research, as well as service to the college and community. Marian University is an institution that values innovative teaching, advising and mentoring. All faculty participate in mentoring, with other related duties as assigned. Teaching responsibilities include teaching in-person courses, as well as contributing to our online programs, as demand requires. Candidates should exhibit skill and enthusiasm in teaching undergraduates and developing innovative experiential learning opportunities in the surrounding community. Primary Responsibilities: Be available to teach at our Fond du Lac, Wisconsin campus. Teach courses throughout the curriculum in the undergraduate Social Work Program in on-campus / in-person, online, and hybrid modes. Example courses include Field Seminars, Social Work Practice, Social Welfare Policy, Social Work Research, Human Behavior in the Social Environment, and Introduction to Social Work. Engage in professional or academic activities in campus-based, local, regional or broader communities in an effort to make a positive impact and advance the recognition and reputation of Marian University. Be actively involved in student mentoring, assessment and assurance of learning, and curriculum design and revision. Assist post-graduate relationship, networks, and establishment of external industry relations to promote programs to employers, secure ongoing placement channels and initiate collaborations. Strictly honor the privacy, security and confidentiality of student records and other sensitive information according to state, federal, and college regulations, policies and procedures. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s in Social Work from a Council on Social Work Education (CSWE) accredited program; terminal degree in the discipline is preferred. Candidates who expect to teach practice courses should also have at least two years of post-MSW practice experience. Willingness to support the Mission and Core Values of Marian University. Preferred qualifications include: Ph.D. in Social Work. ABD and demonstration of effective teaching experience will be considered. Belong to related professional groups/memberships Experience with higher education teaching, both in-person and online modalities. Experience in learning management system platforms. To apply, please submit a letter of interest, a curriculum vita, a statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial copies of transcripts, and the names, email address and telephone numbers of three references to [email protected] . Please place “Adjunct Professor, Social Work” in the subject line of the email. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. EOE/Minorities/Females/Vet/Disabled Transforming lives through academic excellence, innovation and leadership. Marian University is a community committed to learning, dedicated to service and social justice, and joined together by spiritual traditions. Any offer of employment will be contingent upon the receipt of criminal background and reference check information; and the determination that the candidate remains eligible and suitable for employment. Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800-262-7426 [email protected] Follow Us #Fightbluefight Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Tour Employment Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Privacy Policy Title IX Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800.262.7426 [email protected] Follow Us #Fightbluefight Toggle Navigation Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Visit Employment Privacy Policy Title IX Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Page load link Go to Top"
    },
