    "https://www.marianuniversity.edu/assistant-mens-bowling-coach/": {
      "title": "Assistant Men’s Bowling Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Men’s Bowling Coach - Marian University Skip to content en | es Alumni Founder’s Day Give Host Your Event Marian Cares MyMarian Request Info Sabre Café Virtual Tour search field Alumni Founder’s Day Give Host Your Event Marian Cares MyMarian Request Info Sabre Café Virtual Tour Academics Study Area Business Criminal Justice Education Liberal Arts Math & Science Nursing, Human Services and Healthcare By Degree Level Undergraduate Graduate Minors Licenses & Certificates Campus Online Registrar Apply Now Admission Undergraduate Direct Admit Common Application Apply Online Ways To Earn College Credit AP CLEP IB Graduate Online Returning International Students Veterans and Military Veterans Military Withdrawal and Refund Post-Graduation Job Opportunities Recruiting, Marketing, and Advertising Transfer Students Accepted Transfer Credits Ways to Earn College Credit Admitted Students Early College Credit Transferology Cost and Aid Cost of Attending Undergraduate Online Undergraduate Adult Graduate Financial Aid Determining Eligibility Applying for Aid Your Offer Receiving Aid Accepting Loans Paying Your Bills Maintaining Eligibility Canceling or Changing Your Aid Federal Financial Aid Changes FAFSA Financial Aid Policies Return of Federal Funds Tuition Refund Satisfactory Academic Progress Financial Aid Fraud Scholarships & Grants Graduate Aid Working Families Program Partnership Discounts Net Price Calculator Forms & Resources FAQ Athletics Student Life Health & Wellness Counseling Nurse Emergency Care Student Health Insurance Student Organizations Spiritual Life Diversity and Inclusion Student Store Residence Life/Housing & Dining Housing Dining Parking Orientation Student Services Academic Resources First-Year Students Honors Program Learning & Writing Center Institutional Review Board (IRB) Math Placement Library Research Databases & Guides Research Tips Library Services Circulation Policy Copyright Policy Privacy and Confidentiality Policy Selection and Acquisitions Policy Guest Use Policy TRIO Office of Student Success Career & Professional Development Koonce Scholars Program Accessibility Resources About Marian Accreditation and Approvals Campus Map Directory Employment Founder’s Day History Media Kit Mission and Values News President Special Events State Authorization Student Consumer Information Title IX Title IX Support and Appeals Travel University Profile Assistant Men’s Bowling Coach Brad Greenwood 2026-06-17T12:35:08-05:00 Position Title: Assistant Men’s Bowling Coach FTE: .475 FTE (up to 19 hours a week) Department: Athletics Reports To: Director of Athletics/Head Bowling Coach FLSA: Exempt This position promotes and supports the learning experience of Marian University students by assisting the Head Coach in all phases of our men’s bowling program within compliance of Marian University and the appropriate men’s bowling governing bodies. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Assistant Men’s Bowling Coach In collaboration with the head coach, the assistant coach develops and maintains a system to identify prospective student-athletes. Communicates and networks with high school and club coaches Assist in monitoring student athlete academic progress. Assist the head coach with all game day responsibilities. Serve as a role model for the student athletes by continuously exhibiting ethical and professional conduct. Assist in monitoring the conditioning and training of the student athletes Assist in instructing student-athletes on high expectations for academic achievement; monitors the academic progress of student-athletes. Assist in instructing student-athletes on high expectations for student-athlete social responsibility and works to develop well-rounded student-athletes. Assist in instructing student-athletes on a standard of proper student-athlete conduct, both in and out of the athletic arena and works with the Director of Athletics to sanction those who do not meet the set standard. Assist in instructing student-athletes on a standard of proper safety. Monitors condition of equipment and facilities, and reports items in need of repair/maintenance to Instructs student-athletes on a standard of proper student-athlete conduct. Assist in scouting future opponents. Maintains a positive work environment by cooperating in a professional manner with the University community. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, and SKILLS REQUIRED: Bachelor’s degree required, Master’s preferred Able to demonstrate professional development in coaching, collegiate level game knowledge, and a passion for teaching Candidate must demonstrate knowledge of NCAA Division III philosophy, recruitment, rules and regulations Must have willingness to work nights and weekends Candidate must demonstrate great organizational skills in addition to writing and computer skills, interpersonal communication skills, and leadership abilities Experience with “recruiting software” preferred. Valid driver’s license is required Willingness to support the Mission and Core Values of the University. Physical Requirements: While performing the duties of the job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear.  The employee frequently is required to stand, walk, use hands to find, handle or feel, and reach with hands and arms and lift up to 25lbs. To apply, please submit a cover letter, resume, and name, address and telephone number of three references to [email protected] . Please use “Assistant Men’s Bowling Coach” in the subject line of the email. Applications received by July 1, 2026, will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue, thereafter, until the position is filled. EOE/Minorities/Females/Vet/Disabled Transforming lives through academic excellence, innovation and leadership. Marian University is a community committed to learning, dedicated to service and social justice, and joined together by spiritual traditions. Any offer of employment will be contingent upon the receipt of criminal background and reference check information; and the determination that the candidate remains eligible and suitable for employment. Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800-262-7426 [email protected] Follow Us #Fightbluefight Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Tour Employment Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Privacy Policy Title IX Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800.262.7426 [email protected] Follow Us #Fightbluefight Toggle Navigation Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Visit Employment Privacy Policy Title IX Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Page load link Go to Top"
