dvertisement cookies are used to provide visitors with customised advertisements based on the pages you visited previously and to analyse the effectiveness of the ad campaigns. Cookie _twpid Duration 1 year 24 days Description Description is currently not available. Cookie _twsid Duration 1 year 24 days Description Description is currently not available. Cookie taxitag_main__sn Duration 1 year Description Description is currently not available. Cookie taxitag_main__se Duration 1 hour Description Description is currently not available. Cookie taxitag_main__ss Duration 1 hour Description Description is currently not available. Cookie taxitag_main__st Duration 1 hour Description Description is currently not available. Cookie taxitag_main_ses_id Duration 1 hour Description Description is currently not available. Cookie taxitag_main__pn Duration 1 hour Description Description is currently not available. Cookie taxitag_main_v_id Duration 1 year Description Description is currently not available. Cookie taxitag_main_dc_visit Duration 1 year Description Description is currently not available. Cookie taxitag_main_dc_event Duration 1 hour Description Description is currently not available. Cookie taxitag_main_dc_region Duration 1 hour Description Description is currently not available. Cookie __ss Duration 1 day Description This cookie is set by SharpSpring, a marketing automation platform. This is used for tracking visitors and form submissions. Cookie __ss_referrer Duration 1 hour Description This cookie is set by SharpSpring, a marketing automation platform. This is used for tracking visitors and form submissions. Cookie koitk Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description This cookie is set by SharpSpring, a marketing automation platform. This is used for tracking visitors and form submissions. Cookie _gcl_au Duration 3 months Description Google Tag Manager sets this cookie to experiment advertisement efficiency of websites using their services. Cookie __ss_tk Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description This cookie is set by SharpSpring, a marketing automation platform. This is used for tracking visitors and form submissions. Cookie barometric[cuid] Duration 1 year Description Claritas sets this cookie to collect visitor statistics. This data is used to categorize users and improve the effectiveness of website advertising. Cookie personalization_id Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Twitter sets this cookie to integrate and share features for social media and also store information about how the user uses the website, for tracking and targeting. Cookie muc_ads Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Twitter sets this cookie to collect user behaviour and interaction data to optimize the website. Cookie bcookie Duration 1 year Description LinkedIn sets this cookie from LinkedIn share buttons and ad tags to recognize browser IDs. Cookie bito Duration 1 year 1 month Description Beeswax sets this cookie as a unique ID for the visitor, which allows third-party advertisers to target the visitor with relevant advertisements. This pairing service is provided by third-party advertisement hubs, which facilitate real-time bidding for advertisers. Cookie bitoIsSecure Duration 1 year 1 month Description Beeswax sets this cookie to display the user relevant content and advertisements. The service is provided by third-party advertisement hubs, which facilitate real-time bidding for advertisers. Cookie _fbp Duration 3 months Description Facebook sets this cookie to store and track interactions. Cookie barometric[idfa] Duration past Description Claritas sets this cookie to collect visitor statistics. This data is used to categorize users and improve the effectiveness of website advertising. Cookie CDNPHPSESSID Duration session Description Description is currently not available. Cookie WFESessionId Duration session Description No description available. Cookie test_cookie Duration 15 minutes Description doubleclick.net sets this cookie to determine if the user's browser supports cookies. Cookie IDE Duration 1 year 24 days Description Google DoubleClick IDE cookies store information about how the user uses the website to present them with relevant ads according to the user profile. Cookie _mkto_trk Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description This cookie, provided by Marketo, has information (such as a unique user ID) that is used to track the user's site usage. The cookies set by Marketo are readable only by Marketo. Cookie _uetsid Duration 1 day Description Bing Ads sets this cookie to engage with a user that has previously visited the website. Cookie _uetvid Duration 1 year 24 days Description Bing Ads sets this cookie to engage with a user that has previously visited the website. Uncategorised Other uncategorised cookies are those that are being analysed and have not been classified into a category as yet. No cookies to display. Reject All Save My Preferences Accept All Powered by Skip to content en | es Alumni Founder’s Day Give Host Your Event Marian Cares MyMarian Request Info Sabre Café Virtual Tour search field Alumni Founder’s Day Give Host Your Event Marian Cares MyMarian Request Info Sabre Café Virtual Tour Academics Study Area Business Criminal Justice Education Liberal Arts Math & Science Nursing, Human Services and Healthcare By Degree Level Undergraduate Graduate Minors Licenses & Certificates Campus Online Registrar Apply Now Admission Undergraduate Direct Admit Common Application Apply Online Ways To Earn College Credit AP CLEP IB Graduate Online Returning International Students Veterans and Military Veterans Military Withdrawal and Refund Post-Graduation Job Opportunities Recruiting, Marketing, and Advertising Transfer Students Accepted Transfer Credits Ways to Earn College Credit Admitted Students Early College Credit Transferology Cost and Aid Cost of Attending Undergraduate Online Undergraduate Adult Graduate Financial Aid Determining Eligibility Applying for Aid Your Offer Receiving Aid Accepting Loans Paying Your Bills Maintaining Eligibility Canceling or Changing Your Aid Federal Financial Aid Changes FAFSA Financial Aid Policies Return of Federal Funds Tuition Refund Satisfactory Academic Progress Financial Aid Fraud Scholarships & Grants Graduate Aid Working Families Program Partnership Discounts Net Price Calculator Forms & Resources FAQ Athletics Student Life Health & Wellness Counseling Nurse Emergency Care Student Health Insurance Student Organizations Spiritual Life Diversity and Inclusion Student Store Residence Life/Housing & Dining Housing Dining Parking Orientation Student Services Academic Resources First-Year Students Honors Program Learning & Writing Center Institutional Review Board (IRB) Math Placement Library Research Databases & Guides Research Tips Library Services Circulation Policy Copyright Policy Privacy and Confidentiality Policy Selection and Acquisitions Policy Guest Use Policy TRIO Office of Student Success Career & Professional Development Koonce Scholars Program Accessibility Resources About Marian Accreditation and Approvals Campus Map Directory Employment Founder’s Day History Media Kit Mission and Values News President Special Events State Authorization Student Consumer Information Title IX Title IX Support and Appeals Travel University Profile Financial Aid Counselor/Advisor Brad Greenwood 2026-06-29T00:17:28-05:00 Position Title: Financial Aid Counselor/Advisor FTE: 1.0 Department: Financial Aid Reports To: Director of Financial Aid with dotted line to VP for Enrollment FLSA: Exempt Position Summary This position promotes and supports the learning experience of Marian University students by, providing support to both the Financial Aid Office and the Office of Admission by processing financial aid and meeting with prospective and current students and parents to educate them on the financial aid process in an effort to recruit and retain qualified students. Essential Functions Counseling/Advising: 50% 1. Advises, counsels, and builds relationships with prospective and current students and families by guiding them through the financial aid application process, need analysis, and informed financial decision-making through multiple modalities (text, phone, in-person, email, and mail). 2. Provides comprehensive advising and counseling to prospective and current students and parents on the availability, application process, eligibility requirements, and types of financial aid, helping them understand options and develop individualized financial plans to support persistence and completion. Financial Aid Program Management 45%: 1. Maintains a working knowledge of financial need analysis and award systems; awards financial aid to new and continuing students in accordance with federal, state, institutional, and other policies and procedures. 2. Conducts verification for freshman and transfer students, new and current. 3. Certifies alternative loans for Marian University students. 4. Maintains a working knowledge of financial aid regulations and PowerFAIDS. 5. Provides counseling and advising to prospective and current students and parents on the availability, process and types of financial aid. 6. Coordinates the creation and preparation of financial aid forms and annual publications as well as website information, specifically in conjunction with freshman and transfer recruitment. 7. Recommends changes to the Counselor Procedure Manual and provides training to staff in areas of responsibility. 8. Management of partnership programs including documentation, process management, and collaboration with individuals associated with partnership. 9. Award financial aid to non-standard term programs, including graduate, online, and flex programs. 10. Maintains confidentiality and security in regard to all information and records. 11. Maintains a positive work environment by cooperating in a professional manner with the University community. 12. Work to continuously improve data-sharing between the Office of Business and Finance and Office of Financial Aid to best serve the needs of the student population. 13. Represent the office of Financial Aid on-campus events such as individual registrations, campus tours, open houses, New Student Registrations, and payment solutions presentations. Other Responsibilities – 5% · Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Education, Experience and skills required: 1. Bachelor’s degree in relevant field. 2. Experience in a college admission and/or work environment. 3. Strong oral and written communication, interpersonal, organizational, planning, and time management skills. 4. Ability to travel and work with students in rural, urban, and metropolitan areas. 5. Ability to work independently to meet deadlines. 6. Must possess a valid driver’s license and register with the University as an authorized driver. 7. Computer proficient in Microsoft Office and Web tools. 8. Ethical comportment and high regard for confidentiality. 9. Willingness to support the mission and core values of the University. 10. Valid driver’s license and reliable transportation, must be able to be an approved Marian driver. 11. Commitment to supporting Marian University’s mission and values. To apply, please submit a cover letter, resume, and name, email address and telephone number of three references to muapplicants@marianuniversity.edu. Please use “Financial Aid Counselor/Advisor” in the subject line of the email. Applications received by July 10, 2026, will receive full consideration. Salary Range: $47K – $57K EOE/Minorities/Females/Vet/Disabled Transforming lives through academic excellence, innovation and leadership. Marian University is a community committed to learning, dedicated to service and social justice, and joined together by spiritual traditions. Any offer of employment will be contingent upon the receipt of criminal background and reference check information; and the determination that the candidate remains eligible and suitable for employment. Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800-262-7426 admission@marianuniversity.edu Follow Us #Fightbluefight Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Tour Employment Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Privacy Policy Title IX Sponsored by the Congregation of Sisters of St. Agnes 45 S. National Ave. Fond du Lac, Wisconsin 54935-4699 800.262.7426 info@marianuniversity.edu Follow Us #Fightbluefight Toggle Navigation Apply to Marian Request Information Donate to Marian Schedule a Visit Employment Privacy Policy Title IX Copyright © 2025 Marian University. Page load link Arabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Hmong Italian Japanese Korean Nepali Portuguese Russian Spanish Swedish Vietnamese en Go to Top"
    },
